31,2,,status,May,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,,status,Minato,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
33,2,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Daisuke,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"The billing is by area, not headcount. Empty desks still cost us 41,000 yen monthly.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Minato,,"The row by the printer is nine decibels louder. Also, chairs take days to adjust properly.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,May,,The pilot floor took four to nine minutes to set up. Last year’s shuffles took two weeks each.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"The plan gives four window seats. Badge records show arrival times vary wildly, from 8 to 10.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"Last spring, sitting close meant we stopped writing notes. The new joiners learned by listening.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@May, if we move desks, it’s 6,200 yen each. Frequent changes will drain the budget.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@Victoria, if we move often, I can’t settle my chair. I need a stable spot.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,May,,"@Minato, I agree. If we rotate, I lose those setup minutes every time. That’s painful.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Daisuke, the listening thing is interesting. But if we don’t assign seats, the early birds get the windows.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Shunichi, that’s the risk. If it’s first-come, first-served, the latecomers get the noisy spots.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Victoria,,We need a layout that minimizes moves. The cost of re-running power is significant.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Minato,,A fixed desk would let me adjust my chair once and keep it. That’s important for my back.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,May,,"If we fix the desks, I save the setup time. But I need to know I’m not stuck in a bad spot.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"If we fix the desks, we can assign the window seats to those who need them, or rotate fairly.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"If we fix the desks, we can choose who sits next to whom. That feels safer for the team.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Victoria,,I’m leaning towards stability. The financial penalty for change is too high.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Minato,,I feel the same. Comfort and stability are key for me.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,May,,I can live with fixed desks if the assignment is fair. I hate the uncertainty of shuffles.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"Let’s propose fixed desks, but with a clear, fair assignment method.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,I agree. I’d rather have a known neighbor than a random one.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
